        "figure_candidates": [
          {
            "figure": "Figure 1",
            "page_1_based": 3,
            "caption": "Fig. 1. Overview of Group-Invariant Skill Discovery (GISD). Our method\nlearns an equivariant mapping ϕF from the state space S to the Group\nFourier space Z. By aligning state transitions with latent skill vectors z in the\ngroup Fourier domain, the discovered skills inherently respect the underlying\ngeometric symmetry. This structure enables generalization: a policy trained\nfor a specific trajectory τ automatically generalizes to any group-transformed\ntrajectory gτ by simply shifting the skill vector along its group orbit to gz.",
